# project: client_rebrand
// Approvers everywhere: client brand director, client CEO, agency creative director.
// Any one of them can veto at any sign-off and send the stage back into revision.
VAR concept_rounds = 0
VAR ceo_revocations = 0

-> discovery

=== discovery ===
Discovery and brand strategy: research, stakeholder interviews, positioning and the strategy platform.
Done when the strategy deck is ready to present to all three approvers.
+ [Strategy ready to present] -> strategy_signoff

=== strategy_signoff ===
Brand director, client CEO and our creative director review the brand strategy.
Any single veto sends it back into revision.
+ [All three approve the strategy] @human -> naming
+ [Any approver vetoes — revise strategy] @human ~loop~ -> discovery

=== naming ===
Generate and refine the name shortlist from the approved strategy.
Done when a shortlist is ready for legal review.
+ [Shortlist ready for legal] -> trademark_check

=== trademark_check ===
Legal trademark check on every shortlisted name; a failed check knocks that name out of the shortlist.
+ [At least one name cleared legal] -> naming_signoff
+ [Whole shortlist failed — redo naming] ~loop~ -> naming

=== naming_signoff ===
Three-way sign-off on the surviving name(s); pick the final name.
+ [All three approve the name] @human -> visual_identity
+ [Any approver vetoes — back to naming] @human ~loop~ -> naming
+ {ceo_revocations < 1} [CEO revokes an earlier approval] @human -> approval_revoked

=== visual_identity ===
Develop visual identity concepts around the approved name and strategy.
Up to three internal concept rounds before we present to the approvers.
~ concept_rounds += 1
+ {concept_rounds < 3} [Run another concept round] ~loop~ -> visual_identity
+ [Present concepts to approvers] -> visual_signoff

=== visual_signoff ===
Three-way review of the presented visual identity direction.
+ [All three approve the visual identity] @human -> guidelines
+ [Any approver vetoes — rework the concepts] @human ~loop~ -> visual_identity
+ {ceo_revocations < 1} [CEO revokes an earlier approval] @human -> approval_revoked

=== guidelines ===
Produce the full brand guidelines: logo system, colour, type, voice, usage rules.
+ [Guidelines drafted] -> guidelines_signoff
+ [Conference deadline at risk] @human -> descope_call

=== guidelines_signoff ===
Three-way sign-off on the full brand guidelines.
+ [All three approve the guidelines] @human -> rollout_assets
+ [Any approver vetoes — revise guidelines] @human ~loop~ -> guidelines
+ {ceo_revocations < 1} [CEO revokes an earlier approval] @human -> approval_revoked

=== rollout_assets ===
Produce the rollout assets for the conference launch: templates, collateral, digital and event materials.
+ [Rollout package ready] -> final_signoff
+ [Conference deadline at risk] @human -> descope_call

=== final_signoff ===
Final three-way sign-off on the rollout package ahead of the annual conference.
+ [All three approve — go for launch] @human -> launch
+ [Any approver vetoes — rework the assets] @human ~loop~ -> rollout_assets
+ {ceo_revocations < 1} [CEO revokes an earlier approval] @human -> approval_revoked

=== approval_revoked ===
The client CEO has revoked a previously granted approval — assumed to happen at most once.
A human routes the work back to whichever stage the revoked approval belonged to.
~ ceo_revocations += 1
+ [Reopen brand strategy] @human ~loop~ -> discovery
+ [Reopen naming] @human ~loop~ -> naming
+ [Reopen visual identity] @human ~loop~ -> visual_identity
+ [Reopen brand guidelines] @human ~loop~ -> guidelines

=== descope_call ===
The conference launch date is at risk. The brand director chooses what gets descoped to protect the date.
+ [Descope agreed — continue with reduced scope] @human ~loop~ -> rollout_assets
+ [No descope needed — resume guidelines as planned] @human ~loop~ -> guidelines

=== launch ===
The rebrand launches at the client's annual conference.
-> END
